    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0146" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg58"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72116/629: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-08T18:00:00+00:00"
                            >January 8, 1919—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Your 326, November 22, 6 p.m.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d48-f1"/> I have today
                    received a communication from the Minister for Foreign Affairs stating that the
                    Belgian Government is not disposed to comply with the request of the Bavarian
                    Government to send a mission of prominent Bavarians to Belgium to establish the
                    amount of destruction committed by German troops during the war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
